{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here today because your dialysis access isn't working well, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. My peritoneal dialysis isn’t clearing my blood well anymore, and doing all these exchanges is exhausting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You’ve been doing nightly cycler treatments plus two manual exchanges during the day. That’s a lot to manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I’d really like to switch to hemodialysis if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can do that. You already have a left arm fistula from before your transplant, but the recent fistulogram showed poor blood flow and some blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not ready to use? I thought since it was there, it would just work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:23:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s there, but the artery feeding it is narrowed, and there are side branches stealing blood flow. We need to fix that surgically."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:24:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that make it usable for dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:25:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the plan is to revise the fistula—ligate the side branches and re-route the blood flow so it works better for dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And this will be done today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2157-08-28 16:28:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll go to the operating room shortly. The surgeon will make sure your radial pulse stays intact and fix the inflow issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2157-08-28 19:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The surgery went well. They found the radial artery near the fistula was completely blocked, so they moved the inflow and tied off a large side branch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2157-08-28 19:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the fistula working now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2157-08-28 19:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s a good thrill— that buzzing feeling—so blood is flowing well. That’s a great sign for future dialysis use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2157-08-28 19:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I was worried it wouldn’t work after all this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2157-08-28 19:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your hand overnight to make sure there’s no pain, numbness, or circulation issues. So far, everything looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve done well overnight—no complications. The dressing is clean, and we still hear a good bruit and feel the thrill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you. You’ll go back to your regular peritoneal dialysis schedule for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When can I start using the fistula for hemodialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It needs time to mature—usually 4 to 6 weeks. The access clinic will follow up to check readiness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call if you have fever, pain, numbness, or a cold or blue hand. Also, check daily for the thrill. If it’s gone, call immediately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should keep the arm protected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:11:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly—no blood pressures, no IVs, no heavy lifting, and avoid tight clothes or jewelry on that arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2157-08-29 09:14:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Your medications stay the same, and the dressing comes off in a few days. Gentle washing is okay, but no soaking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2157-08-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home. Follow up with the access clinic soon, and keep monitoring your fistula."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2157-08-28 16:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2157-08-29 11:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease, previously on peritoneal dialysis, was admitted for revision of a non-functional left radiocephalic arteriovenous fistula due to poor inflow and multiple stenotic areas. She desired transition to hemodialysis as her current regimen was burdensome. She underwent surgical revision with ligation of side branches and re-routing of inflow due to complete stenosis of the radial artery proximal to the anastomosis. The procedure was successful, with palpable thrill and audible bruit postoperatively. She remained stable overnight without complications and was discharged home with instructions to monitor the access site, protect the arm, and follow up with the access clinic. Her home medications were continued without changes.",
    "problems": [
      "Mechanical complication of other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Surgical operation with anastomosis, bypass, or graft, with natural or artificial tissues used as implant causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Anemia in chronic kidney disease",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Mitral valve insufficiency and aortic valve insufficiency",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified anomaly of urinary system",
      "Personal history of tobacco use",
      "Long-term (current) use of antiplatelet/antithrombotic",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits"
    ]
  }
}
